<section class="about-section">
  <h1>about the work</h1>
  <p>The work at Lucid Vagary moves between image and language. Image-poems pair a poem with a photograph or drawing so that each reads through the other.</p>
  <p>Drawings and sketches explore eyes, faces, masks, hands, and inner landscapes, often recurring across years and series such as <a href="/posts/The-Pentaptych-of-Growth/">The Pentaptych of Growth</a>.</p>
  <p>See a selection of <a href="/sketchbook/">sketchbook pages</a>.</p>
  <p>Some pieces carry personal histories; <a href="/posts/the-city/">The City on the Lake</a>, for example, was written at the site of the author's hemorrhagic stroke.</p>
